<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<srmd:SimulationResourceMetaData xmlns:srmd="http://ssp-standard.org/SSPTraceability1/SimulationResourceMetaData" xmlns:ssc="http://ssp-standard.org/SSP1/SystemStructureCommon" xmlns:stc="http://ssp-standard.org/SSPTraceability1/SSPTraceabilityCommon" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" version="1.0.0" name="SSP-Model SRMD" generationTool="orchideo | easySSP (eXXcellent solutions GmbH)" generationDateAndTime="2025-09-03T19:07:53Z" data="SimulationTask.stmd" checksum="2711141E587F708EFB805148FCDD9009235CCB81745E517048EAEFC4C647A2C5" checksumType="SHA3-256">
    <stc:Classification type="org.prostep.csp-framework" xlink:type="simple">
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="verification.model-component-fit.target.level" xlink:type="simple" type="">4</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="verification.model-component-fit.status.level" xlink:type="simple" type="">2</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="cred-assessment-sim.contact-name" xlink:type="simple" description="Comment as text" type="">Hubertus Tummescheit, hubertus.tummescheit@modelbased.cloud</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="cred-assessment-sim.product-name" xlink:type="simple" description="Comment as text" type="">EV Project InfiniRange    </stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="cred-assessment-sim.project-name" xlink:type="simple" description="Comment as text" type="">InfiniRange Powertrain Development Gate 2</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="cred-assessment-sim.question-of-interest" xlink:type="simple" description="Comment as text" type="">Everything related to improving the Vehicle range under standard drive cycle conditions. Special focus is on torque arbitration, where a higher degree of generative braking should improve range. Current brake blending is considered too "timid" in using the e-machine when possible. </stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="cred-assessment-sim.simulation-task" xlink:type="simple" description="Comment as text" type="">* Quantify the potential gain through more aggressive brake blending
* Quantify deviations from standard conditions for 4 representative climate zones in terms of thermal passenger comfort (cold, moderate, hot and dry, hot and humid)
* Evaluate corner cases for controller design: long, steep ascent and descent in mountains.
* The influence on battery aging on range and performance </stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="cred-assessment-sim.simulation-domain" xlink:type="simple" description="Comment as text" type="">Combination of electrical, mechanial and thermal: we are looking at overall vehicle energy management</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="cred-assessment-sim.context-of-use" xlink:type="simple" description="Comment as text" type="">- The context of use is the standardized product definition stage preliminary range evaluation process. 
- The model may be suitable for similar range determination simulations that don't require detailed thermal models. 
- The model can be used as a starting point (Experiment definitions, KPI definitions) for range simulations in the ''detailed development'' stage.</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="cred-assessment-sim.quantities-of-interest" xlink:type="simple" description="Comment as text" type="">* Vehicle range estimate for different climate zones and thermal loads, for all vehicle variants. </stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="verification.code.numerical-code-verification.activity.status.level" xlink:type="simple" description="Values: 0-4" type="">3</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="verification.code.numerical-code-verification.activity.target.level" xlink:type="simple" description="Values: 0-4" type="">3</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="verification.code.numerical-code-verification.activity.comment" xlink:type="simple" description="Comment as text">Library components have been thoroughly validated. Parameters to be validated before next gate</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="verification.code.software-quality-assurance.activity.status.level" xlink:type="simple" description="Values: 0-4" type="">3</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="verification.code.software-quality-assurance.activity.target.level" xlink:type="simple" description="Values: 0-4" type="">4</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="verification.code.software-quality-assurance.activity.comment" xlink:type="simple" description="Comment as text">Vendor executes and documents regular testing for every release and minor update, and shares it.</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="verification.calculation.numerical-solver-error.activity.status.level" xlink:type="simple" description="Values: 0-4" type="">4</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="verification.calculation.numerical-solver-error.activity.target.level" xlink:type="simple" description="Values: 0-4"/>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="verification.calculation.numerical-solver-error.activity.comment" xlink:type="simple" description="Comment as text">All simulations are done with error-controlled adaptive solvers with a tolerance of at least 1e-6. This is adequate by company code verification standards</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="verification.calculation.discretization-error.activity.status.level" xlink:type="simple" description="Values: 0-4" type="">N.A.</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="verification.calculation.discretization-error.activity.target.level" xlink:type="simple" description="Values: 0-4" type="">N.A.</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="verification.calculation.discretization-error.activity.comment" xlink:type="simple" description="Comment as text">Not applicabel for lumped parameter models.</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="verification.calculation.model-component-fit.activity.status.level" xlink:type="simple" description="Values: 0-4" type="">3</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="verification.calculation.model-component-fit.target.level" xlink:type="simple" description="Values: 0-4" type="">4</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="verification.calculation.model-component-fit.comment" xlink:type="simple" description="Comment as text">CModel fit has been established by extensive testing during vendor selection process for all library components.</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="verification.user-error-analysis.user-errors.activity.status.level" xlink:type="simple" description="Values: 0-4" type="">3</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="verification.user-error-analysis.user-errors.activity.target.level" xlink:type="simple" description="Values: 0-4" type="">4</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="verification.user-error-analysis.user-errors.activity.comment" xlink:type="simple" description="Comment as text">User errors are unlikely, with a hgihly prescriptive, documented simulation process, regular user training, and code and result review of all simulation results.</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="validation.computational-model.model-form-analysis.activity.status.level" xlink:type="simple" description="Values: 0-4" type="">3</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="validation.computational-model.model-form-analysis.activity.target.level" xlink:type="simple" description="Values: 0-4" type="">4</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="validation.computational-model.model-form-analysis.activity.comment" xlink:type="simple" description="Comment as text">Model form has been decided to be adequate during vendor selection process. Results are documened in ''VendorEvaluationAssessment''</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="validation.computational-model.data-quality-analysis.activity.status.level" xlink:type="simple" description="Values: 0-4" type="">3</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="validation.computational-model.data-quality-analysis.activity.target.level" xlink:type="simple" description="Values: 0-4" type="">4</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="validation.computational-model.data-quality-analysis.activity.comment" xlink:type="simple" description="Comment as text">At this stage, no prototype test data is available. Comparison with predecessor model data shows small and reasonable deviations. </stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="validation.computational-model.model-sensitivity-quantification.activity.status.level" xlink:type="simple" description="Values: 0-4" type="">3</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="validation.computational-model.model-sensitivity-quantification.activity.target.level" xlink:type="simple" description="Values: 0-4" type="">3</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="validation.computational-model.model-sensitivity-quantification.activity.comment" xlink:type="simple" description="Comment as text">Model sensitivity w.r.t. aging and environment temperature is the the core purpose of this model. Model sensitivity w.r.t. parameter variations from manufacturing tolerances will be analyzed at a later stage. In this early phase, a 2% absolute deviation is kept as a safety margin w.r.t. hard constraints.  
		</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="validation.computational-model.model-uncertainty-quantification.activity.status.level" xlink:type="simple" description="Values: 0-4" type="">3</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="validation.computational-model.model-uncertainty-quantification.activity.target.level" xlink:type="simple" description="Values: 0-4" type="">4</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="validation.computational-model.model-uncertainty-quantification.activity.comment" xlink:type="simple" description="Comment as text">Uncertainty quantification is doen systematically for all 3rd party component parameters, and the propagation through the system is computed through extensive simulations based on Sobol space filling quasi-random draws from the uncertain space. Uncertainty quantification for all upstream parameters is prescribed in supplier instructions for component model parameterization.</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="validation.comperative-data.test-condition-suitability.activity.status.level" xlink:type="simple" description="Values: 0-4" type="">3</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="validation.comperative-data.test-condition-suitability.activity.target.level" xlink:type="simple" description="Values: 0-4" type="">4</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="validation.comperative-data.test-condition-suitability.activity.comment" xlink:type="simple" description="Comment as text">Not applicable in this phase for the system level. </stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="validation.comperative-data.test-condition-uncertainty.activity.status.level" xlink:type="simple" description="Values: 0-4" type="">N.A.</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="validation.comperative-data.test-condition-uncertainty.activity.target.level" xlink:type="simple" description="Values: 0-4" type="">3</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="validation.comperative-data.test-condition-uncertainty.activity.comment" xlink:type="simple" description="Comment as text">System level tests are for next phase only. </stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="validation.comperative-data.test-sample-suitability.activity.status.level" xlink:type="simple" description="Values: 0-4" type="">N.A.</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="validation.comperative-data.test-sample-suitability.activity.target.level" xlink:type="simple" description="Values: 0-4" type="">4</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="validation.comperative-data.test-sample-suitability.activity.comment" xlink:type="simple" description="Comment as text">Not applicable.</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="validation.comperative-data.test-sample-uncertainty.activity.status.level" xlink:type="simple" description="Values: 0-4" type="">N.A.</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="validation.comperative-data.test-sample-uncertainty.activity.target.level" xlink:type="simple" description="Values: 0-4" type="">4</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="validation.comperative-data.test-sample-uncertainty.activity.comment" xlink:type="simple" description="Comment as text">Not applicable.</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="validation.applicability.qoi-evaluation.activity.status.level" xlink:type="simple" description="Values: 0-4" type="">2</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="validation.applicability.qoi-evaluation.activity.target.level" xlink:type="simple" description="Values: 0-4" type="">3</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="validation.applicability.qoi-evaluation.activity.comment" xlink:type="simple" description="Comment as text">The objective quantities of interest (range) are evaluated by standard drive cycle simulations. The somewhat subjective one of brand-authentic driving feel is evaluated by test drivers during final control parameter calibration. </stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="validation.applicability.cou-evaluation.activity.status.level" xlink:type="simple" description="Values: 0-4" type="">1</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="validation.applicability.cou-evaluation.activity.target.level" xlink:type="simple" description="Values: 0-4" type="">3</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="validation.applicability.cou-evaluation.activity.comment" xlink:type="simple" description="Comment as text">Context of use is documented in this SRMD's cred-assessment-sim.context-of-use entry (standardized product-definition-stage preliminary range evaluation); formal evaluation against CoU acceptance criteria is scheduled for the Gate 2 review recorded in DecisionTask.dtmd.</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="validation.assessment.output-comparison.activity.status.level" xlink:type="simple" description="Values: 0-4" type="">2</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="validation.assessment.output-comparison.activity.target.level" xlink:type="simple" description="Values: 0-4" type="">4</stc:ClassificationEntry>
        <stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="validation.assessment.output-comparison.activity.comment" xlink:type="simple">Simulation range results compared against the InfiniRange predecessor platform's field data within a 3% deviation band; full physical-prototype comparison for this model generation is scheduled for the next development gate.</stc:ClassificationEntry>
    </stc:Classification>
