  <stc:Classification type="org.mic-core.sic-core"><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="administrative.simulation-task">ArchitectureLevelRange -- WLTP/NEDC range-sensitivity simulation task (SimulationTask.stmd)</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="administrative.simulation-task.confidentiality">Company confidential, plus Need-to-know Tier 1 suppliers</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="administrative.contact.customer-person">R. Halvorsen, VP Powertrain Programs</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="administrative.contact.customer-entity">MBI LLC - Vehicle Programs</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="administrative.contact.contractor-person">T. Okafor, Senior Simulation Engineer</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="administrative.contact.contractor-entity">MBI LLC - Vehicle Energy Systems CAE</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="administrative.overall-product">EV Project InfiniRange</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="administrative.specific-product">InfiniRange Powertrain, Gate 2 configuration</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="administrative.ordering-project">InfiniRange Powertrain Development Gate 2</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="administrative.simulation-request">Gate 2 range/efficiency substantiation request -- see DecisionTask.dtmd AnalyzeDecisionTask</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="administrative.simulation-task.date.start">2026-06-01</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="administrative.simulation-task.date.delivery">2026-08-04</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="administrative.simulation-task.creator">T. Okafor</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="administrative.simulation-task.date.creation">2025-09-03</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="analysis.item-under-test">EV powertrain torque-arbitration control strategy and battery-variant lineup</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="analysis.simulation-task.objectives">Quantify combined WLTP/NEDC range gain from more aggressive regenerative-brake blending, across 4 battery variants</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="analysis.engineering-task.higher-level">InfiniRange Gate 2 tooling-release decision</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="analysis.engineering-task.specific">Torque-arbitration control strategy and battery sizing selection</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="analysis.simulation-task.further-requirements">See SimulationTask.stmd, RequirementsPhase</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="analysis.quality-aspects">Independent QA review at each phase gate, per SimulationTask.stmd DefineQualityAssuranceRequirements</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="analysis.verification">Numerical solver tolerance &lt;=1e-6; library components previously code-verified (see verification.code.* entries above)</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="analysis.validation">Comparative validation against InfiniRange predecessor field data within a 3% deviation band</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="requirements.parameter.subject-information.parametrized-entity">Battery pack (SoC_max, capacity variant), e-machine (P_nom, w_nom), torque-arbitration thresholds</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="requirements.model.purpose-objectives">Architecture-level EV range estimation under WLTP/NEDC drive cycles</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="requirements.model.subject-information.modeled-entity">EV powertrain: e-machine, converter, battery, torque arbitration, driver, ambient</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="requirements.model.effects-considered">Electrical/mechanical/thermal lumped losses; regenerative braking; ambient-temperature effects</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="requirements.model.further-model-requirements">See SimulationTask.stmd DefineModelRequirements and each model's own MTMD</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="requirements.parameter-value-distribution-function">Supplier-declared tolerance bands treated as uniform distributions for UQ sampling</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="requirements.test-case">Baseline, aggressive-regen, degraded-battery -- see SimulationTask.stmd DefineTestCaseRequirements</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="requirements.simulation-environment">FMI 2.0 Co-Simulation, Optimica Compiler Toolkit, adaptive solver tolerance 1e-6</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="requirements.simulation-integration">2-level hierarchical SSD: Controllers subsystem plus top-level range model</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="requirements.model.confidentiality">Company confidential, plus Need-to-know Tier 1 suppliers</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="requirements.model.quality-requirements">Model-component-fit target level 4 (see verification.model-component-fit entries above)</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="requirements.parameter.confidentiality">Company confidential</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="requirements.parameter.quality-requirements">Supplier-sourced parameters must carry documented uncertainty bounds</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="requirements.test-case.confidentiality">Company confidential</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="requirements.test-case.quality-requirements">Must bound best- and worst-case range-gain claims (fresh vs. aged battery)</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="requirements.simulation-environment.quality-requirements">Solver tolerance &lt;=1e-6 per company code-verification standard</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="requirements.simulation-integration.quality-requirements">Connector unit/type consistency verified across all ssd:Connections</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="requirements.quality-assurance">Independent verification review at Requirements and Design phase gates</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="requirements.verification">See SimulationTask.stmd VerifyRequirements</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="design.model">ElectricRange_V2 reused unchanged; TorqueControl extended with AgressiveRegeneration variant -- see each model's MTMD DesignPhase</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="design.parameter">5 battery/controller variant combinations, see SimulationTask.stmd DefineParameterDesignSpecification</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="design.test-case">simulation1/2/3 run folders, see SimulationTask.stmd DefineTestCaseDesignSpecification</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="design.simulation-environment">Optimica Compiler Toolkit, CVode-class adaptive solver, tolerance 1e-6</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="design.simulation-integration">Controllers subsystem wired to top-level ElectricRange_V2-1 component, per SystemStructure.ssd</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="implementation.model">See ElectricRange_V2.mtmd and TorqueControl.mtmd ImplementationPhase</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="implementation.parameter">5 parameter-set variants committed in SystemStructure.ssd / EVRangeExampleNEDC.ssd ssd:ParameterBindings</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="implementation.test-case">3 config.json execution definitions under extra/org.ssp-standard.ssp-traceability.stmd/simulationN/</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="implementation.simulation-environment">7 FMI 2.0 CoSimulation FMUs, Optimica Compiler Toolkit, generated 2025-08-17 to 2025-08-28</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="implementation.simulation-integration">SystemStructure.ssd (WLTP) and EVRangeExampleNEDC.ssd (NEDC), both SSP 2.0.1 schema-valid</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="implementation.simulation-integration.settings">Co-Simulation coupling, variable-step communication, per each FMU's modelDescription.xml defaults</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="implementation.model.confidentiality">Company confidential, plus Need-to-know Tier 1 suppliers</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="implementation.model.quality">0 defects in setup QA memo, see SimulationTask.stmd AssureSimulationSetupQuality</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="implementation.parameter.confidentiality">Company confidential</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="implementation.parameter.quality">Cross-checked against ssd:ParameterBindings, see ImplementParameter</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="implementation.test-case.confidentiality">Company confidential</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="implementation.test-case.quality">3 of 3 test cases executed and post-processed successfully</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="implementation.simulation-environment.quality">Environment pinning confirmed against packaged modelDescription.xml, see ImplementSimulationEnvironment</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="implementation.simulation-integration.quality">0 defects, see AssureSimulationSetupQuality / DeriveSimulationSetupQualityVerdict</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="execution.model">EVExample.FMUs.Intermediate.ElectricRange_V2 (top-level), TorqueControl.fmu and WLTPDriver.fmu/Driver.fmu (Controllers subsystem)</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="execution.parameter">Standard battery variant (baseline+aggressive regen runs), DegradedStandardBatteryL2 (worst-case run)</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="execution.tool">Modelon Impact co-simulation orchestration, per SimulationTask.stmd ExecuteSimulation Procedure</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="execution.test-case">simulation1 (baseline), simulation2 (aggressive regen), simulation3 (degraded battery)</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="execution.data">results.csv / results_sampled.csv per run, see ExecuteSimulation Output</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="execution.tool.settings">Variable-step adaptive solver, tolerance 1e-6, full WLTP cycle duration per run</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="evaluation.results">+5.1% to +6.8% combined-cycle range gain from aggressive regen blending, see DeriveSimulationQualityVerdict</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="fulfillment.task-status">Approved -- objective fulfilled, see DecideSimulationObjectiveFulfillment</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="fulfillment.objectives">Primary range-gain KPI met with margin; thermal/corner-case/battery-aging objectives partially addressed, flagged for next gate</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="fulfillment.evidence">SimulationTask.stmd EvaluationPhase outputs, cross-referenced in DecisionTask.dtmd EvaluateResults</stc:ClassificationEntry><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="fulfillment.date">2026-08-01</stc:ClassificationEntry></stc:Classification>
</srmd:SimulationResourceMetaData>